                    "line": 929,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thu Nguyen",
                        "email": "thu@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "ThuBaNguyen"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we avoid to use anti-pattern in log message:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/anti-patterns.md#ill-defined-data-structuring-in-lg2-message-strings"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_fw_update_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 929,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "pldmtool is a CLI based utility, not a service/daemon. Using phosphor-logging for this tool would introduce unnecessary dependencies and could clutter the journal logs.\n\nAre there any existing examples in OpenBMC where phosphor-logging is used for CLI-based tools ?"
                }
            ],
